 @ZipMapp  Why you would want to exclude the elephant? Because that's the intent of the study. It was designed to see if it could find evidence that biology doesn't affect long-term differences. It was the intent of the study to exclude it from the debate. It was trying to answer the question. 
While it's certainly not a reliable study for developed countries other than Denmark, it's still showing that you likely didn't even check out the study.

Yet you immediately get overly defensive about it. As you have been throughout this entire comment thread.

 @GoodChoicess  "Sharing a thought" isn't the same as making a factual claim. A factual claim requires sourcing in order to prevent misinformation from being spread. If you're too lazy to provide a source, then you're actively being part of the social decline that misinformation on the internet is known for. 

It's ironic though, you're praising ZipMapp because what that person said reaffirms your desire to be lazy, while ZipMapp has nonstop criticized laziness on the internet. 
Although ZipMapp has done so from the standpoint of a logical fallacy, the desire to prevent laziness on the internet is still praiseworthy.

